WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.600
Apple is rethinking

00:00:01.411 --> 00:00:02.519
Mac permissions for

00:00:02.331 --> 00:00:03.357
AI agents

00:00:03.894 --> 00:00:05.155
AI agents like

00:00:04.967 --> 00:00:06.299
Meta's Muse request

00:00:06.111 --> 00:00:07.608
extraordinary access

00:00:07.668 --> 00:00:08.445
messages

00:00:08.635 --> 00:00:09.353
email

00:00:09.425 --> 00:00:10.202
photos

00:00:10.274 --> 00:00:11.747
browsing history and

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:12.372
then act on

00:00:12.184 --> 00:00:13.033
your behalf

00:00:13.558 --> 00:00:14.807
One user Matt

00:00:14.619 --> 00:00:15.126
Robb

00:00:15.221 --> 00:00:16.128
found Muse had

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.001
been given permission

00:00:16.813 --> 00:00:18.003
to send messages

00:00:17.815 --> 00:00:18.841
containing his home

00:00:18.652 --> 00:00:20.020
address to strangers

00:00:20.558 --> 00:00:21.949
On November 16

00:00:22.197 --> 00:00:23.753
Apple announced macOS

00:00:23.565 --> 00:00:25.475
27.3 beta 2

00:00:25.723 --> 00:00:26.654
where supported

00:00:26.808 --> 00:00:27.421
you can pick

00:00:27.233 --> 00:00:28.600
exactly which protected

00:00:28.412 --> 00:00:29.272
folders an app

00:00:29.084 --> 00:00:29.933
may access

00:00:30.016 --> 00:00:31.076
instead of all

00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:31.760
or nothing

00:00:32.286 --> 00:00:33.300
Full story on

00:00:33.111 --> 00:00:34.007
the dashboard
